---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Website & Enquiry Terms | Unit Alfa"
  description="Terms for using Unit Alfa’s manufacturing website, viewing component examples and submitting a request for quotation."
>
  <PageIntro
    label="WEBSITE INFORMATION"
    title="WEBSITE & ENQUIRY TERMS."
    intro="Component examples help describe our work. The agreed drawing and written quotation define an individual requirement."
  />
  <article class="container legal-copy section-bottom">
    <h2>Manufacturing information</h2>
    <p>
      Product photographs show examples of Unit Alfa’s work. Machine ratings are not a general
      guarantee of achievable part size, thickness, tolerance, output or delivery time. Material,
      inspection, tooling, finish and supply scope are established through technical review.
    </p>
    <h2>Requests for quotation</h2>
    <p>
      Submitting an enquiry or receiving a reference confirms receipt by the website service. It is
      not an order acceptance, quotation or manufacturing commitment. Estimated annual quantities
      are planning information, not an automatic purchase obligation. Commercial terms are agreed
      separately in writing.
    </p>
    <h2>Drawings and confidentiality</h2>
    <p>
      Only submit files you are entitled to share for assessment and quotation. Contact the company
      before uploading if a separate confidentiality agreement is required. Keep your private status
      link secure and avoid sending credentials or unrelated personal information.
    </p>
    <h2>Company material</h2>
    <p>
      The Unit Alfa logo and company photographs remain the property of their respective owners.
      Customer names identify relationships stated by Unit Alfa and do not imply endorsement of this
      website. Company imagery and technical content are excluded from the source-code licence.
    </p>
    <h2>Status information</h2>
    <p>
      The enquiry tracker shows updates entered by authorised staff. It is separate from the
      company’s internal production systems and does not provide live machine or production-order
      monitoring.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
